{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>He shall not search, etc.</b> Since it says ״וְכֹל מִבְחַר נִדְרֵיכֶם״ (Deuteronomy 12), one might think he could select and take out the best one — Scripture says, ״לֹא יְבַקֵּר בֵּין טוֹב לָרַע״ — whether whole or blemished, sanctity rests upon it. And this is not to say that a blemished animal may be offered; rather, it is eaten in the manner of tithe, and it is forbidden to shear or work it (see Bekhorot 14)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:09:02.179997465Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}